    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1582">

                <pb facs="1275" n="1159" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.00/432.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-16T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 16, 1912—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Nearly all the supervisors have been heard from. They report satisfactory and
                    orderly elections on 14th, Diaz party not voting.</p>
                <p>Yesterday rowdies in Panama committed numerous outrages, none so far as known
                    upon Americans. I have impressed upon Minister for Foreign Affairs urgent
                    necessity for promptly stopping this, which is apparently countenanced by the
                    police.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
